2.
Definitions.
- In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
"appointed day" means the date of coming into force of this Act;
(b)
"brackish water land" means any land inundated with or subject to inundation by salt water and fit for pisciculture;
(c)
"licensing authority" means Brackish Water Fish Farmers Development Agency (BFDA) Goa registered under the
Societies Registration Act, 1860;
(d)
"Government" means the Government of the State of Goa;
(e)
"prescribed" means prescribed by rules made under this Act;
(f)
"Tribunal" means the Administrative Tribunal constituted under the Goa, Daman and Diu Administrative Tribunal Act,
1965 (Act
6 of 1965
).
